-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Initial Proportion:** The initial number of negative Gaussians is critical. Too few or too many can degrade optimization efficacy [S1].
-*   **Precision:** The quadratic minimization for null density requires careful handling of the positive semi-definiteness of matrix $A$ [S1].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If $h_i = 1$ and $m_{1,i} = m_{0,i}$, the solution for $w_i$ is any real number, indicating a direction of invariance [S1].
+### Parameters
+*   **Initial Negative Ratio:** The initial number of negative Gaussians is a critical hyperparameter. The optimal value is typically set to approximately 20% of the total Gaussians during initialization [S1].
+*   **Hyperparameter Tuning:** The numbers of positive and negative components are treated as hyperparameters and adapted through grid search during cross-validation [S1].
 
